* =====================================================================================================
* ldo_3v3__rt9080.lib -- behavioural model of the Richtek RT9080 (fixed-output, TSOT-23-5, no SNS pin)
*
* Part:       RT9080-33GJ5 (U1, main board, VSYS -> +3V3). The output option is a parameter (VNOM), so a
*             wrong variant in the BOM (e.g. RT9080-28GJ5) is simulated with the right output voltage.
* Datasheet:  Richtek DS9080-09, December 2024
*             https://www.richtek.com/assets/product_file/RT9080/DS9080-09.pdf
* No vendor SPICE model is published for the RT9080 (checked richtek.com and distributor listings,
* 2026-10), so this is a hand-built macro model. Every number below cites the datasheet table or
* figure it comes from. "Fig." means the Typical Operating Characteristics (DS section 16, pages 8-11).
*
* MODELLED
*   Output voltage   VNOM*(1+ACC). ACC is the accuracy corner, +/-2 % (Table 14, ILOAD = 1 mA, TA = 25 C).
*   Temp drift       Typical drift vs 25 C from Fig. "Output Voltage vs Temperature" (VOUT = 3.3 V):
*                    3.277 V @ -40 C, 3.301 @ -10, 3.320 @ 25, 3.328 @ 60, 3.329 @ 75. Fit:
*                    dV = 0.42 mV/C*(T-25) - 4.8 uV/C^2*(T-25)^2 (3.3 V option), scaled by VNOM/3.32.
*   Line regulation  LINE = fraction of VOUT over the spec span VNOM+1 .. 5.5 V: 0.13 % typ, 0.35 % max
*                    (Table 14, 1.8 V <= VIN <= 5.5 V). Sign is a corner (+/-). Extrapolated below VNOM+1 V,
*                    where Table 14 gives no accuracy/regulation guarantee (DS conditions VOUT+1 < VIN < 5.5).
*   Load regulation  LREG = 0.5 % typ, 1 % max for 1 mA < ILOAD < 600 mA (Table 14). Sets the DC loop
*                    transconductance GDC = 0.6 A / (LREG*VNOM).
*   Dropout          PMOS on-resistance RDS = 0.517 ohm typ (0.31 V / 0.6 A) and 0.883 ohm max (0.53 V / 0.6 A),
*                    Table 14 "Dropout Voltage, 3 V <= VOUT", 25 C. RDSK = 1 (typ) or 1.71 (max).
*                    Temperature: +0.28 %/C from Fig. "Dropout Voltage vs Temperature" (VOUT 3.3 V, 600 mA:
*                    250 mV @ -40 C, 305 @ 25, 390 @ 125). Gate drive: RDS scales as 2.7 V/(VIN-0.9 V), fitted to
*                    the Table 14 dropout rows for the lower output options (VIN = VOUT + VDROP: 1.33 ohm @ 1.93 V,
*                    1.18 @ 2.06, 0.95 @ 2.2-2.5, 0.68 @ 2.7, 0.60 @ 3.1, 0.517 @ 3.6).
*   Current limit    ILIM 1.1 A typ / 610 mA min (Table 14, VOUT = 90 %). Fig. "Current Limit vs Temperature"
*                    gives ~0.98 A for the 3.3 V option at 25 C. Fold-back to IFB ~0.72 A at VOUT -> 0 V
*                    (Fig. "Fold-Back Current Limit vs Temperature", 3.3 V; section 18.3 "around 0.6 A").
*                    Linear between VOUT = 0 and 90 % of VNOM.
*   Enable/UVLO      EN rising threshold 0.67 V (Fig. "Enable Threshold vs Input Voltage", VIN >= 2 V;
*                    Table 14 VEN_R 0.9 V max). Operating input 1.2 V min (Recommended Operating Conditions);
*                    the model is off below VINMIN = 1.2 V (behaviour there is not specified).
*   Soft start       Exponential reference ramp, tau TSS = 70 us typ, read from Fig. "Power On from EN"
*                    (VIN 4 V, VOUT 3.3 V: 67 % at ~65 us, 92 % at ~195 us, 98 % at ~390 us). No min/max given.
*   Quiescent        IQ 2 uA typ / 4 uA max at ILOAD = 0 (Table 14). Load-dependent GND current from
*                    Fig. "Ground Current vs Load Current" (VIN 4.3 V, VOUT 3.3 V, 25 C): 57 uA @ 1 mA, 105 @ 10 mA,
*                    205 @ 50 mA, 270 @ 100 mA, 760 @ 600 mA. Between 0 and 1 mA the DS gives nothing: the model
*                    interpolates linearly (ASSUMPTION, bench-verify the sleep current).
*   Discharge        80 ohm output pull-down when disabled (Table 14 RDISCHG, section 17.7).
*   Body diode       VOUT -> VIN (abs max VOUT - VIN <= 0.3 V, section 10). No reverse channel current.
*   Loop dynamics    Two-path error amplifier (fast proportional path GHF + slow high-gain path GLF with time
*                    constant TAU1) followed by one pole FA, output-voltage referred, scaled by the feedback
*                    factor beta = 0.8 V/VNOM (block diagram: 0.8 V reference + internal divider). Fitted to
*                    Fig. "Load Transient" (RT9080-08, VIN 1.8 V, 1 mA -> 600 mA, ~20 us edges, COUT 1 uF):
*                    undershoot ~27 mV, overshoot ~23 mV, recovery ~10-20 us, settled offset ~5 mV.
*                    GHF1 = 20 S, TAU1 = 5 us, FA = 5 MHz (beta = 1 basis). The fit is checked by
*                    test_ldo_3v3.py::test_model_matches_datasheet_figures.
*   PSRR feedthrough GRO = 8.4 mS (VIN -> VOUT conductance) sets PSRR = 75 dB at 1 kHz (Table 14: VIN 3 V,
*                    VOUT 2.5 V, 50 mA, COUT 1 uF). GFF/TFF = gate-coupling high-pass, fitted to Fig. "Line
*                    Transient" (VIN 2.8 -> 3.8 V, VOUT 1.8 V, 1 mA: spikes about +4.6 / -3 mV).
*
* NOT MODELLED
*   Over-temperature shutdown (150 C, 20 C hysteresis): junction temperature is computed in the test from
*   theta-JA(EVB) 100.7 C/W (DS section 13) instead. Output noise. Dropout-region IQ increase (not
*   characterised). IQ / GND current vs temperature and vs VIN (only 25 C, VIN 4.3 V curves exist).
*   Exact internal compensation (unpublished): the dynamic fit reproduces the DS figures at the DS
*   conditions only; dynamic results with other capacitors are indicative, not guaranteed.
*   Gate slew in dropout recovery (internal amplifier saturation) is approximated by clamping the slow path
*   to ILIM/GLF (anti-windup ASSUMPTION). Soft-start spread and EN threshold spread (only typ curves exist).
*
* Pins: VIN EN VOUT GND
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt LDO3V3_RT9080 VIN EN VOUT GND params: VNOM=3.3 ACC=0 TEMPC=25 RDSK=1 LREG=0.005 LINE=0.0013
+ ILIM=0.98 IFB=0.72 IQ=2u TSS=70u RDIS=80 VENTH=0.67 VINMIN=1.2 GHF1=4 TAU1=50u FA=600k GRO=8.4m
+ GFF=30m TFF=1u SLOW=1
.param BETA={0.8/VNOM}
.param GDC={0.6/(LREG*VNOM)}
.param GHF={BETA*GHF1}
.param GLF={max(GDC-GHF, 0.01)}
.param XL={ILIM/GLF}
.param DVT={(0.42e-3*(TEMPC-25) - 4.8e-6*(TEMPC-25)*(TEMPC-25))/3.32}
.param RDS0={0.517*RDSK*(1+0.0028*(TEMPC-25))}
.param TAUA={1/(6.283185*FA)}
* enable (EN threshold and minimum operating input), 0..1
Bena ena 0 V = 0.25*(1+tanh((V(EN,GND)-VENTH)/0.02))*(1+tanh((V(VIN,GND)-VINMIN)/0.02))
Rena ena 0 1G
* set point: accuracy corner, temperature drift, line regulation (extrapolated outside VNOM+1..5.5 V)
* (the DC line-regulation term is low-passed at 16 Hz so that it does not mask the AC PSRR of Table 14)
Bln lnt 0 V = LINE*(V(VIN,GND)-(VNOM+1))/(5.5-(VNOM+1))
Rln lnt lnr 10Meg
Cln lnr 0 1n
Bset set 0 V = VNOM*(1+ACC)*(1+DVT)*(1 + V(lnr))*V(ena)
* soft start: exponential reference ramp, tau = TSS
Rss set ss {TSS/1n}
Css ss 0 1n
* error (output referred)
Berr err 0 V = V(ss) - V(VOUT,GND)
Rerr err 0 1G
* adaptive bias: loop transconductance and amplifier pole scale with the amplifier bias, taken as the GND
* current IQ + IG(I), normalised to its 600 mA value (758 uA). IG(I) = 0.3m*I^0.25*(1-exp(-I/0.3 mA)) + 0.82m*I
* is a smooth fit of Fig. "Ground Current vs Load Current" (within -13..+3 % from 1 to 600 mA); below 1 mA
* it follows a near-linear fade to 0 (no DS data there, ASSUMPTION)
* (bias follows its target with a 1 us lag, which breaks the algebraic ip -> bias -> ip loop)
Gbias 0 bias cur = ((IQ + (3.0e-4*pow(V(ip)*V(ip)+1e-14, 0.125)*(1-exp(-abs(V(ip))/0.3m)) + 8.2e-4*abs(V(ip))))/758u - V(bias))*1n/1u
Cbias bias 0 1n
Rbias bias 0 1T
* slow high-gain path: first-order lag TAU1, target clamped (anti-windup)
Gx1 0 x1 cur = (max(min(V(err), XL), -XL) - V(x1))*1n/TAU1/SLOW
Cx1 x1 0 1n
Rx1 x1 0 1T
* control current (A, as a voltage). The amplifier pole FA also scales with the bias (weak gate drive at
* light load); its target is clamped (anti-windup)
Gctl 0 ctl cur = (max(min(GHF*V(err) + GLF*V(x1), 1.5*ILIM), -0.2) - V(ctl))*1n/TAUA/SLOW
Cctl ctl 0 1n
Rctl ctl 0 1T
* pass device: smooth min of demand, current limit with fold-back, and the triode (dropout) limit
Brds rds 0 V = RDS0*2.7/max(V(VIN,GND)-0.9, 0.3)
Rrds rds 0 1G
Blim lim 0 V = IFB + (ILIM-IFB)*max(min(V(VOUT,GND)/(0.9*VNOM), 1), 0)
Rlim lim 0 1G
Btri tri 0 V = (V(VIN,GND)-V(VOUT,GND))/V(rds)
Rtri tri 0 1G
* demand = amplifier control current + PMOS output conductance (DC PSRR) + gate-coupling high-pass
* (HF line feedthrough); the loop trims ctl to cancel the last two at low frequency
Rlp VIN vlp {TFF/1n}
Clp vlp GND 1n
* (GRO and GFF are calibrated at 50 mA and scale with the bias, as g_ds and g_m of the PMOS scale with its
* current; bias(50 mA) = 203u/758u = 0.268)
Bdem dem 0 V = V(ctl) + V(bias)/0.268*(GRO*(V(VIN,GND)-V(VOUT,GND)) + GFF*(V(VIN,GND)-V(vlp,GND)))
Rdem dem 0 1G
Bm1 m1 0 V = 0.5*(V(dem)+V(lim) - sqrt((V(dem)-V(lim))*(V(dem)-V(lim)) + 1e-6))
Rm1 m1 0 1G
Bmn mn 0 V = 0.5*(V(m1)+V(tri) - sqrt((V(m1)-V(tri))*(V(m1)-V(tri)) + 1e-6))
Rmn mn 0 1G
* no reverse channel current: soft clamp at 0 (softplus, 1 uA knee)
Bip ip 0 V = V(ena)*0.5*(V(mn) + sqrt(V(mn)*V(mn) + 1e-12))
Rip ip 0 1G
Bpass VIN VOUT I = V(ip)
* ground current: IQ plus the load-dependent part IG(I), shutdown 0.1 uA (Table 14 ISHDN)
Bgnd VIN GND I = V(ena)*(IQ + (3.0e-4*pow(V(ip)*V(ip)+1e-14, 0.125)*(1-exp(-abs(V(ip))/0.3m)) + 8.2e-4*abs(V(ip)))) + (1-V(ena))*0.1u
* active discharge when disabled
Bdis VOUT GND I = (1-V(ena))*V(VOUT,GND)/RDIS
* PMOS body diode
Dbody VOUT VIN LDO3V3_DBODY
.model LDO3V3_DBODY D(IS=1e-12 N=1.2 RS=0.2)
.ends LDO3V3_RT9080
